{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03245",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.25,
      "end_seconds": 5.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Mm, good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.78,
      "end_seconds": 14.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.2,
      "end_seconds": 23.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.75,
      "text": "Mainly ringing in the ears. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.05,
      "end_seconds": 29.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.84,
      "end_seconds": 34.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "I'm on tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.89,
      "end_seconds": 45.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.0,
      "end_seconds": 63.73,
      "duration_seconds": 17.73,
      "text": "It's been going on for about a week. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I did try to ignore it for a while. Oh, and no dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.55,
      "end_seconds": 69.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Any hearing better in a noisy room as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.67,
      "end_seconds": 78.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "Mm, yes. Sorry, what was I saying, about hearing better in a noisy room, mostly mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.07,
      "end_seconds": 99.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Have you had any discharge, ear pain or facial weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.11,
      "end_seconds": 104.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Erm, no, no discharge, ear pain or facial weakness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.49,
      "end_seconds": 110.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.95,
      "end_seconds": 113.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.98,
      "end_seconds": 122.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.45,
      "end_seconds": 128.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Yes, I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.81,
      "end_seconds": 133.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.16,
      "end_seconds": 144.86,
      "duration_seconds": 10.7,
      "text": "Erm, I have an enlarged prostate, for about a year. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.68,
      "end_seconds": 154.88,
      "duration_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "Right, yes, an enlarged prostate is known to us, good to have that clear. Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.5,
      "end_seconds": 157.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.37,
      "end_seconds": 163.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.09,
      "end_seconds": 167.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.09,
      "end_seconds": 180.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.15,
      "end_seconds": 183.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.61,
      "end_seconds": 191.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.71,
      "end_seconds": 196.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.33,
      "end_seconds": 199.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.69,
      "end_seconds": 204.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.6,
      "end_seconds": 208.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.03,
      "end_seconds": 222.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.49,
      "end_seconds": 242.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Okay: temp 37.0 degrees, BP is 125 over 80, heart rate 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.96,
      "end_seconds": 245.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.35,
      "end_seconds": 248.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.75,
      "end_seconds": 253.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.47,
      "end_seconds": 255.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.3,
      "end_seconds": 270.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Both ear drums look normal and the tuning fork is heard better through the bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.36,
      "end_seconds": 290.73,
      "duration_seconds": 15.37,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. So, based on the history and the examination, I think we're dealing with a conductive hearing loss, possibly otosclerosis at this stage. We shouldn't forget wax."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.92,
      "end_seconds": 298.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Actually, uh, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.44,
      "end_seconds": 331.14,
      "duration_seconds": 30.7,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a conductive hearing loss, possibly otosclerosis, and we'll know more once the a hearing test is back. We should do a hearing test for hearing loss. We should do a CT scan of the ears for possible otosclerosis. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. A hearing aid or an operation are both options after the tests."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.88,
      "end_seconds": 348.55,
      "duration_seconds": 15.67,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I'd like you back after the tests. Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.51,
      "end_seconds": 354.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "So, I come back after the tests. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.11,
      "end_seconds": 359.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.02,
      "end_seconds": 364.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.53,
      "end_seconds": 367.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "So, goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}